::Q1::What does a fact table primarily store?
{ 
~Only database connection settings
~Only descriptive information about customers
=Measurable business events and their numeric measures
~Only report titles
}

::Q2::Which columns are measures in the example Fact_Sales table? 
{
=quantity and revenue
~customer_id and date_id
~sale_id and product_id
~customer_id and product_id
}

::Q3::What is the purpose of foreign keys in a fact table? 
{
=They reference related dimension tables that provide context
~They replace all numeric measures
~They prevent dimension tables from existing
~They store only calculated report titles
}

::Q4::What does the grain of a fact table describe? 
{
=Exactly what one row in the fact table represents
~The total number of reports created
~The physical size of the database server
~The number of dimensions in a schema
}

::Q5::Why are dimension tables useful in analytical queries? 
{
=They provide descriptive context for measures stored in fact tables
~They prevent filtering and grouping
~They store only raw application logs
~They replace every fact table measure
}